00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.620
Chapter 4 Shadow

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.110
This is awful! Someone!

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.950
Fire!

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.070
Someone call the fire brigade!

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.580
Would you like some water?

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.760
Here you go.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.050
What a terrible commotion. Was it a fire?

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:47.700
Yesterday, there was a fire
and someone was killed.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.100
It's been just awful.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.440
Killed?

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.370
A street murder.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.900
A night buckwheat noodle
vendor was cut down.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.490
And there was a fire in Gion
just the other day, too.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.410
Man, why do I have to
do something like this?

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.250
Here, eat.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.340
Hey, stop!

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.780
You bastard!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.060
I finished feeding them.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.650
You stink. Go wash your face!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.660
Where's your response?!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.500
Yes, sir!

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.780
Your work's not done yet.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:43.570
Understood, sir!

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.830
That's some tough work.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.340
Looks like Toshi's being
pretty hard on him.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.000
No, this is fine. He's
the new guy, after all.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.520
This kind of work is to be expected.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.700
I didn't...

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.550
I didn't join up to do things like this!

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.350
Hello, there!

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.060
Hey, little one, come to spar?

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:03.900
Whoops! You're an impatient one.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.320
Now, hold on a second!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.750
You can't spar with a
wooden sword against a spear.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.790
Whoa!

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.670
Damn it!

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.250
That's right, keep your arms in!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.380
Step in quickly!

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.220
You've got a pretty good knack for this!

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.320
You could become strong if you practice!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.790
Face!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.770
Ow! That doesn't mean you
can leave yourself open.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.230
Yo! Sano! Shinpachi!

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.030
Same as ever, I see.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.150
Yo, Heisuke!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.700
When did you get back?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.030
We missed having our third joker around.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.970
Who are you calling a joker?

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.120
By the way, I heard
Mr. Hijikata took on a page?

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.420
How cute is he?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.660
Thing is, I haven't seen
anyone that fits the description,

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.050
so I've been looking for him.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.220
But I'll bet he's a real pretty boy!

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.100
Restraining my imagination,
sort of like this.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:17.660
Mr. Hijikata wouldn't go for anyone less
than beautiful, even if he was solicited!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.160
He unilaterally assigned
the boy to be his page!

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.730
Not a word of complaint, even though
the boy's bad at making tea!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.780
To top it off, if he let the boy in
because he's like Soji, well then...

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.660
Heisuke!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.620
I'm sorry, but blow your nose and
forget about that image right away.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.080
I don't follow.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.160
I get it! He's good in bed!

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.410
You're free to yell whatever you like,

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.710
but if Mr. Hijikata heard
that, he'd kill you.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.670
The correct answer is over here!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.930
This is the much-rumored
no-good page, Tetsunosuke Ichimura.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:00.730
He's cute! He's real cute!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.690
What?!

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.120
Wow! This head and these short limbs!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.540
The spitting image of a puppy!

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.030
Who're you calling a puppy?!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.290
He's still so small,
even when he struggles!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.080
But did Mr. Hijikata's tastes
run along these lines?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.790
Don't fan the flames.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.700
Oh, sorry.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.920
Ichimura, was it? I guess I
haven't introduced myself yet.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.700
I'm Heisuke Todo.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.390
I'm an old-timer here from back
when we were at Shiei Hall.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:31.220
And I technically serve directly
under the Vice Commander.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.760
Oh, but I'm young.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.080
I'm a complete nut when
it comes to cute things,

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.370
but I'm pretty good with a sword.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.520
Nice to meet you!

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.640
Sure, nice to meet you too.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.150
Mr. Kondo, the trio of jokers
are all here for once.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.790
Ah, so Todo's back.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.490
What happened to Yamanami?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.410
He's apparently staying in Shimabara today.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.660
Saying he wanted to see Akesato,
since it's been so long.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.160
That's not it.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.420
It's an excuse for him to delay
seeing me again, even by one day.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.750
You're still saying that, Toshi?

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.120
But it's too bad.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.830
I want to tell Mr.
Yamanami about Tetsu, too.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.080
He likes children, so I'm
sure he'll welcome Tetsu.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.640
Unlike someone else...

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.480
Excuse me.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.450
Ah, Yamazaki, what is it?

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.280
Has the Choshu Clan made some kind of move?

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.690
No, it's a report concerning a matter
the Vice Commander is investigating.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.410
Details of the fires that have been
occurring these past few months.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.200
There have been thirty-four
fires up to April of this year,

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.950
of which twenty-one have
been vacant houses.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.130
And in the dead of night,
when there aren't even lanterns lit.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.550
No doubt about it.
Toshimaro Yoshida is here.

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.120
Yoshida?!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.830
A disciple of Shoin Yoshida,
who was executed in the Ansei Purge.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.660
In the Choshu Clan,
along with Shinsaku Takasugi,

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.410
he's said to be one of Shoin's
three brightest students.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.400
He's big.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:11.320
Then, the man behind these
arsons is most likely Yoshida.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.200
Exactly.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.080
The crazy pyromaniac bastard!

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.700
I am very sorry.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.830
The men who carried out the

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.080
Masuya

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.080
mission the other day blundered.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.330
I do not care.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.330
One or two more corpses will
not make much of a difference.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.620
Yes, sir.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:32.750
So, to what tasks shall I assign those
who have newly arrived in Kyoto?

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.670
Have them go sightseeing or something.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:35.840
Sir?

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:40.560
Meaning, learn their way around so as
not to get eaten by the Wolves of Mibu.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.200
Here you are.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.500
Ah, thank you.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.980
I have my shop to tend to,
so please excuse me.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.940
Master, how much longer
must we sit still in this place?!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.580
I have already waited for a
considerable amount of time,

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:00.830
ever since I started to follow you!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.870
When will the hunt begin?!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.200
Do not be impatient, Suzu.
The prey is not going anywhere.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:10.960
We can take our time hunting, burning,
and slowly smoking them out.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.950
Tell me what you've been doing.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:36.580
I was sparring, sir.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.740
Who told you to go to the training hall?!

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:42.120
Why do I have to do things like this?!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.330
It seems you still don't understand
the position you're in.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:50.300
As punishment, copy the Strictures
of the Shinsengumi 100 times over!

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:58.660
Damn it! I'll quit being his page!

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.760
Hey! Hurry, hurry!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.140
Mr. Okita is?!
It's your loss if you miss this!

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.060
What the...?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.330
<i>A Choshu spy or something?</i>

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.330
<i>Why are they drawing
swords at headquarters?</i>

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:50.870
<i>No, more importantly...</i>

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.330
<i>This bloodlust...</i>

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:55.700
<i>Mr. Okita isn't showing a single opening!</i>

00:11:58.750 --> 00:11:59.650
He's good.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:01.950
Vice Commander!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.910
I haven't felt this in a long time.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.830
It's refreshing, if it's
just every so often.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.250
What are you saying?

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:27.700
White.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.700
If you'd at least switch to
a red loincloth or something,

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.980
perhaps you would seem a little more manly?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.040
What about you, Hajime?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.560
With that black, it's
practically a funeral.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.790
Tetchan, didn't you know?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:53.410
No, I didn't. I haven't seen
that guy around until now.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:56.200
Hajime Saito, Third Unit Captain.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.800
He's always been around.
It's just that you didn't notice.

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:04.630
Can't be helped. That Hajime
doesn't really stand out usually.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:08.090
No matter where he is, he's always
just kind of there in the crowd.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.100
But he's good!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.730
If he and Mr. Okita went at it,
they'd probably both end up dead.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.060
Excellent insight.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:24.080
Hajime's right up there with Okita
when it comes to his swordsmanship.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.830
Here, of course, even among the
assassins against the Shogunate,

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.830
about the only ones who could
win against him one-on-one

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.330
are guys who wouldn't die even when
they've been stabbed through the heart.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.540
But you know, he's got
no motivation at all.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.960
And there's <i>that</i>.
Yeah, <i>that</i>.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:42.410
If he's that good, hurry up
and introduce me to him sooner.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:47.840
Oh-ho, so the Vice Commander's page has been
granted authority to demand such things?

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.830
When did you...?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.540
I can see a dark shadow behind you.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:59.270
Mightn't you be troubled by that shadow?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:06.700
Now...

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.740
I have some business to
take care of, so pardon me.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.410
Wait!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.950
Speak with respect to your superiors!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.370
Yes, sir!

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.750
Incidentally, might you be hungry?

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.420
I want some buckwheat noodles.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.350
About what we were talking about earlier...

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.730
Thank you for the food.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:43.940
Mr. Saito!

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.160
An assassination took place here.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.290
The time was one year ago.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.620
Here too.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.890
A murder in the name of
heavenly punishment.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.000
His age was eighteen.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.370
His name was Matsugoro Hayashi.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:35.290
He was framed for a crime he
did not commit by a close friend

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.120
and came to Kyoto, abandoning his homeland.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.700
However, being a ronin,
he found no place to call home,

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.540
so he apparently lost all hope in the world
and committed suicide in this vacant house.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.250
You can see?

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.790
Indeed!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:54.550
I can hear the voices of beings not of
this world and sense their thoughts.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:58.910
At times, I can even speak with them.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:03.600
However, I cannot converse
with your shadow.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:09.080
I do not know who it is, but it
means that he is still alive.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.700
Leaving the grounds without
permission, dereliction of duty,

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.200
fleeing from punishment...

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.500
Brat, do you remember the
Strictures of the Shinsengumi?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.160
You don't mean seppuku?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.420
I can't very well demand that, but...

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.250
No dinner tonight!
You will stand guard all night!

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:31.130
Yes, sir.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.290
Mr. Hijikata sure was mad.

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.640
Oh? Mr. Saito?

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.850
Now, with this night's game,
how many will we have played?

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.140
It has already exceeded
a thousand, my lord.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:34.240
Behold! The exclusionists
have won the capital this night.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.580
I am most awed and humbled, my lord.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.910
Then I shall show you an interesting plot.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.330
My <i>shiki </i>are already keeping
a keen eye on their movements,

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:52.160
but my lord, please watch at your
leisure from where you are now.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:59.410
It is a matter that no longer concerns me.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.870
With Saneakira no longer of this world,

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:05.310
whether the capital burns
or falls to ruin...

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:11.830
Yes, gazing upon the land falling
to ruin will surely be most amusing.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:16.620
The exclusionist loyalists and the
Wolves of Mibu may both wreak havoc.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:21.000
The barbarians may trample
this divine land as well.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:26.160
I shall see this land's demise with you.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:38.260
Who's there?

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.140
The malice is still in the air.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.800
Of evil spirits, or of man?

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.700
Well, well, a member of the Shinsengumi.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.560
A tasty morsel has found
its way into the trap.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.450
<i>This late at night?</i>

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:41.950
I make a rule of not crossing
swords with the possessed.

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:00.920
Mr. Saito?

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.660
So, you're the one!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:39.330
A good moon, is it not?
We shall meet again.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.010
Damn, he got away.

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.450
Tetsunosuke, I appreciate
that you came to my aid,

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:52.180
but have you not forgotten
something important?

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.190
Shoot! I'm supposed to stand guard!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:59.580
As you can see, there
is not a scratch on me.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.190
Put your worries to rest and go back.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:04.030
Mr. Saito, excuse me!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.410
What the heck was that?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:16.580
Shinsengumi

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.830
Tetsu? Tetsunosuke?

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:20.600
Are you sure you should be sleeping
so soundly out here, little page?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:24.720
Shoot!

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.040
I am very sorry!

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:31.970
You thought you'd be
forgiven if you apologized?

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.140
What do you take me for?

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.160
If you want to go off and amuse
yourself whenever you want,

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:37.750
there's no need for you to be here.

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.360
Get out of here right now!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.750
Oh, come on, Toshi.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:45.780
Now, now, Tetsunosuke only
joined up recently after all.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.700
And he is showing remorse,

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.160
so I'll make sure to have
a good talk with him later.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.160
I...

00:21:55.660 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>Maiku o nigirishime
hitto pareedo no onpareedo</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.390
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kibun wa doudai?</i>

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>Suteeji orireba sasuga no jentoruman</i>

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:19.450
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kokoro mo kandai!</i>

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:23.360
<i>Jimichi ga yue ni seikatsu sae mo jimi ni</i>

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:27.290
<i>Kotsu-kotsu tsumiagemashou</i>

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.290
<i>Jimichi ni yume ga kanaimasu you ni</i>

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:34.990
<i>Kyou mo, Jimmy, ikimashou</i>

